<title>GERMANY: German government reduces yield on 5-year Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government reduces yield on 5-year Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is lowering the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds by raising the issue price of the paper to 101.20 from 100.80, the Bundesbank said.</p>
<p>The move, effective on December 16, brings the yield on the Series 121 4.75 percent paper to 4.47 percent from 4.56 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
